WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:01.269
- This is how Albert is.

00:00:01.269 --> 00:00:03.832
I mean, he's like a
little doll. (laughing)

00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:08.832
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.682
Albert is three years old.

00:00:10.682 --> 00:00:14.115
He was the runt of the litter
and he was really tiny.

00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:17.053
Albert was on Cat From
Hell for a licking problem,

00:00:17.053 --> 00:00:18.501
and we were also on Animal Planet

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.384
for the show called
America's Next Cat Star,

00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:24.480
and they put a bunch of
cats that are predicted

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.013
to become famous.

00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:27.731
I started his Instagram
account when I went

00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:29.797
to a cat festival.

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:32.427
People were just ooh-ing
and aah-ing over him.

00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:39.074
Albert has not always been famous.

00:00:39.074 --> 00:00:42.104
He's been made famous by heavy marketing.

00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:44.333
Albert's most notable post would be his

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:47.015
moonwalking, where I
put Albert on the window

00:00:47.015 --> 00:00:50.243
ledge and I started filming him.

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:52.170
I was like, Albert come here. (clicking)

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.283
But his butt was facing me, and then

00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:57.127
all of a sudden, he
started walking backwards,

00:00:57.127 --> 00:00:59.879
and I put it up on
Instagram and instantly,

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:01.992
the comments just flooded in.

00:01:01.992 --> 00:01:04.405
It was like everybody was
tagging all their friends.

00:01:04.405 --> 00:01:07.999
(gentle ambient music)

00:01:07.999 --> 00:01:09.600
Albert's costumes are really hard to find

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.828
because you can't really find
that many good pet costumes.

00:01:12.828 --> 00:01:14.848
The ones in pet stores are usually

00:01:14.848 --> 00:01:18.435
low quality so I had to, we get creative.

00:01:18.435 --> 00:01:20.664
We usually shop at Babies
R Us, or try to find

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:23.149
human infant clothes.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.836
So the way we usually do shoots

00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:27.061
is he gets distracted a lot.

00:01:27.061 --> 00:01:28.873
So I put him in a costume.

00:01:28.873 --> 00:01:30.434
We'll have to have some toys.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.250
Albert. (squeaking)

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.606
It's like he knows that
he's being photographed

00:01:35.606 --> 00:01:38.265
so he'll do everything
in his power to look away

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:40.401
from the camera.

00:01:40.401 --> 00:01:42.520
Oh, look at that.

00:01:44.194 --> 00:01:46.549
We do a lot of sponsored posts.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:50.994
The biggest ones we've done
are for Coca-Cola, Walgreens.

00:01:50.994 --> 00:01:53.329
Yeah, and we did one
for the Deadpool movie.

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:55.963
When we first started,
it was very difficult

00:01:55.963 --> 00:01:57.244
of us to get sponsored posts.

00:01:57.244 --> 00:01:57.952
(clicks)

00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:00.175
We were only being
approached by pet companies.

00:02:00.175 --> 00:02:01.952
I worked really hard on Albert's account

00:02:01.952 --> 00:02:03.978
with his photos, and I do this full time

00:02:03.978 --> 00:02:06.038
so I thought why not?

00:02:06.038 --> 00:02:08.227
Why can't we get some sponsors?

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:11.031
At first, we got a lot of
people that didn't understand

00:02:11.031 --> 00:02:13.620
the sponsored content,
especially because he's a cat

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.244
advertising products that
are not related to pets.

00:02:16.244 --> 00:02:18.310
So what people don't
understand is that we love

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.561
doing Albert posts and videos and photos

00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:23.662
but just because we love it doesn't mean

00:02:23.662 --> 00:02:25.276
that we shouldn't get paid for it.

00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:27.167
If people really love
Albert, like they should

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.605
be understanding of
that, that we're putting

00:02:29.605 --> 00:02:30.977
so much work into this.

00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:33.125
We can't afford to do it
for free all the time.

00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:36.166
I worked so hard on getting more followers

00:02:36.166 --> 00:02:38.094
everyday, it's a day to day thing.

00:02:38.094 --> 00:02:40.241
Every single day is me thinking about,

00:02:40.241 --> 00:02:41.681
okay, what's the next step?

00:02:41.681 --> 00:02:45.255
My goal in life is
always to do what I love.

00:02:45.255 --> 00:02:46.904
That's what I've been doing with Albert.

00:02:46.904 --> 00:02:48.687
I love him so much, and it's so much fun

00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:50.648
spending time with him.

00:02:50.648 --> 00:02:53.215
I'm taking videos and photos of him.

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:56.660
I've turned my hobby into a career.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.660
(gentle instrumental music)

